{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"and he was building a city, and he called the name of the city after the name of his son Chanoch\"</b> is that at first he intended to be childless in his iniquity, and after a child was born to him he began to build a city for his son to dwell in. And because he is cursed and his deeds will not prosper, he named it \"Chanoch,\" to indicate that he did not build it for himself, for he has no city or settled dwelling on earth, for he is a wanderer and a fugitive, but rather the building would be for Chanoch, as though Chanoch built it for himself. And because Scripture did not say \"and he built a city,\" as it says \"and he built Nineveh\" (Genesis 10:11), \"and the children of Gad built Dibon\" (Numbers 32:34), it indicates that all his days he was building the city, for his deeds are cursed — he would build a little with toil and labor, and move and wander from that place, and return there and build a little, and not prosper in his ways. And the generations of Cain and his deeds were written to inform that HaShem is slow to anger, and He granted him length of days to beget sons and grandsons, and He mentioned that He visits the iniquity of fathers upon children, and his seed was cut off. And our Sages said (Shemot Rabbah 31:17) that he lived many years and died in the Flood, and He did not bring his old age down to Sheol in peace, but he saw in the destruction both himself and all his seed with him. And the likely explanation is that his generations were only six generations until the Flood, and in the generations of Sheth there were two generations more, or else it was not necessary to recount all of them and Scripture recounted these, to inform who were the ones who began the building of cities and the pasturing of flocks and the art of music and the craft of metals, and it wrote the rebuke of Lemech with his wives to indicate that he begot only sons who were cut off before he begot them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:46.965469863Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}